  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "FY2027 inside guidance (organic sales ~-2%, adjusted operating margin ~10.3%); partial margin recovery of ~1pp by FY2031 from frozen price discipline and Project Catalyst; volumes stabilise and growth settles at ~1.5% nominal; capex normalises from a 5% peak to 3.7%. Value roughly equals today's enterprise value: the market is pricing the reset, not a recovery.",
    "bull": "The reset arrests six years of volume decline by FY2028; GLP-1 lifts portion-controlled frozen meals and protein snacks; Foodservice grows; margin rebuilds to ~18% (still below FY2024's ~21%), leverage reaches the 3x target and the equity re-rates as debt falls.",
    "bear": "Elasticity stays above historical norms, private label and Walmart squeeze staples, GLP-1 is a net headwind for snacks, and revenue shrinks ~11% over five years with margin sliding to ~14%. Leverage stays near 4x; with 4x leverage, a modest enterprise-value miss is a large equity miss."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Conagra is a mature, ex-growth US packaged-food manufacturer carrying ~4x leverage. The FY2026 loss is non-cash impairment, not cash collapse -- normalised EBITDA was ~$1.9bn and owner FCF ~$0.9bn -- but the impairments confirm a lower earning power than the Pinnacle-era base. The valuation therefore normalises earnings to guidance rather than to FY2024-25 margins, caps the terminal at 10-14x FCF with 0-1.5% growth, and weights the bear case at 30% because leverage turns modest operating misses into large equity misses.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Leverage: ~$7.4bn net debt against ~$7.3bn of equity value; every 1x of EV/EBITDA is ~$3.9/share",
      "Volume elasticity on the H2 FY2027 price increases (management says elasticity is running above historical levels)",
      "Walmart concentration (~29% of sales) and private-label share gains in shelf-stable staples",
      "GLP-1 adoption: assumed roughly neutral in base; a net snack headwind is a bear-case driver",
      "Further impairments signal the brand base; Refrigerated & Frozen has no remaining fair-value cushion",
      "Ardent Mills earnings (~$140-180m) are commodity-sensitive and inside the EBITDA path"
    ]
  },
