    "wacc_rationale": "USD flows, USD rate. Risk-free ~4.3% (10y UST), ERP 5.0%, levered beta ~1.0 at ~4x net debt/EBITDA (asset beta of US packaged food ~0.5) gives cost of equity ~9.3%; pre-tax cost of debt ~5.4% (Sep-2026 5.40% notes due 2031) = ~4.1% after tax; market weights ~50/50 (equity ~$7.3bn, net debt ~$7.4bn) -> ~6.7%, rounded up to 7.0%. Same WACC in all three scenarios: risk is charged through the scenario paths and weights, not a stacked premium.",
    "lease_treatment": "US GAAP ASC 842: operating lease cost sits inside cost of goods sold / SG&A, so it is already inside the EBITDA margin path; operating lease liabilities (~$207m at FY2026) are therefore NOT added to net debt. One treatment, applied once. lease_cost_pct_path is zero.",
    "nci_treatment": "No meaningful NCI (FY2026 nil, FY2025 $0.1m).",
    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF (dcf-methods routing: US operating company, consumer staples manufacturer). First valuation of CAG, no prior DCF or memory entry. NORMALISATION: FY2026 statutory operating loss of -$1,628.4m is driven by $2,929.6m of non-cash goodwill ($2,382.4m, Refrigerated & Frozen) and brand ($547.2m) impairments plus a $42.2m divestiture gain; restating for those and restructuring 45.7, legal -37.4, CEO separation 8.1 and environmental 5.4 gives adjusted operating profit ~$1,281m (11.4% margin). Adding D&A 396.0, equity-method earnings 140.7 (+7.5 Ardent Mills restructuring) and SBC 54.7 gives a pre-SBC EBITDA of ~$1,880m = 16.7% of sales (FY2025 same basis ~19.5%, FY2024 ~21%). The EBITDA margin path is on that basis: it INCLUDES Ardent Mills equity earnings (44% JV, pass-through LLC taxed at Conagra level; FY2026 earnings 140.7 roughly equal to cash distributions), so no separate Ardent Mills asset is added in the equity bridge. FY2027 guidance (reaffirmed at Q1 FY2027, 30-Sep-2026): organic sales -1% to -3%, adjusted operating margin 10.0-10.5%, adjusted EPS $1.40-1.50, capex ~$550m, ~$250m debt paydown, leverage ~4x at year end. That maps to ~15.8% pre-SBC EBITDA and 5.0% capex in year 1. The impairments are treated as non-cash and non-recurring, but they are evidence: they record that the Pinnacle brands earn less than they were bought for, which is why the base margin path recovers only partway toward the FY2024-25 level. OWNER FCF: last_fcf = reported FCF 978.7 - SBC incl. equity-award taxes 74.5 - interest income 0 (net debt, no stripping) = 904.2. Reported FCF is post-interest (~$380m interest expense); the engine builds UNLEVERED flows from components and deducts net debt once. NET DEBT: Q1 FY2027 balance sheet (2026-08-30) notes payable 32.5 + current LTD 787.5 + senior LTD 6,940.1 = 7,760.1 less cash 371.6 = 7,388.5. The Metrics CSV TotalDebt of 8,517.5 for Q1 2027 does not tie to the face of the balance sheet and was not used. Pension/OPEB deficits are not deducted (not material to the extracted balance sheet; flag if a later filing shows a large unfunded position). BUYBACKS: $15.3m in FY2026 and $44m in Q1 FY2027 against $54.7m SBC -- the flat count is roughly funded; dividend cut 50% in July 2026 to $0.175/qtr with freed cash going to debt paydown. HORIZON: 10 years, because capex steps down from the 5.0% guided peak and margins recover through ~year 5.",
